{
 "updated": "2026-11-10",
 "about": "Trending on GitHub: open source repos that were going viral recently and help people build apps, games and sites. Refreshed by a daily job: candidates come from public trend lists and articles found with web search (no scraping, no logins), each repo is checked to exist on GitHub and to have a permissive license (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, MPL-2.0, CC0, Unlicense), then scripts/dev/trending-check.js validates this file. \"stars\" is the count reported by the linked trend source on its date (null when none gave one), not a live number. \"seenOn\" lists public posts and articles where the repo was being talked about. Running TribeCode apps fetch this file daily from GitHub (host only) and fall back to the bundled copy.",
